oms could overlap, but blasts in CBC point more strongly to hematologic malignancy", "Metabolic Complication of Diabetes: Glucose is normal, and visual changes are not typical for diabetic ketoacidosis or hyperglycemic crisis", "Hemorrhagic/Thrombotic Event: Mild ataxia and visual changes could suggest stroke, but neurological exam is non-focal and no acute focal deficits"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Blasts in peripheral blood", "Anemia and thrombocytopenia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4970099667774086, "posterior": 0.30539307089008855, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["A subacute clinical course with constitutional symptoms is more typical of chronic myeloid processes (e.g., CML in blast crisis) than de novo AML, which usuall…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16472868217054262, "posterior": 0.39636900476269415, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The combination of blasts in peripheral blood with cytopenias (anemia, thrombocytopenia) is classic for myeloid neoplasms, which typically exhibit marrow failu…"], "evidence_against": ["Lymphoid neoplasms (e.g., ALL) often present with lymphadenopathy and distinct immunophenotype markers, which are absent here. This reduces likelihood for